-- title:
--   Fricke twin: kernel along the branch j - j_q^{ q}
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$, and $a \in k$ with $a^{q^2} = a$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ that is finite over $\mathbb Q$, put $A_0 =$ `coeffSubring A K` $= A \cap K$ with the restricted reduction `redRestrict red K`, and let $\varpi \in A_0$ be such that an element of $A_0$ reduces to $0$ precisely when it is a multiple of $\varpi$. Let $g$ be an element of `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A₀ (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)`, the subring of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the form $r(j,j_q)/s(j,j_q)$ with $r,s \in A_0[X_0,X_1]$ and $s$ not vanishing at $(a,a^q)$ after reduction, where $j,j_q$ are the series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$. Assume the series $g$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full modular function field of that level, and assume (hypothesis $h_2$) that its image under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constants from $A$ together with $j$ and $j_q$ at the complement of the kernel prime of coefficientwise reduction. Then `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red` kills that image if and only if $g$ belongs to the ideal of `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A₀ (redRestrict red K) a (a ^ q)` generated by the two elements obtained by evaluating $\varpi$ and $X_0 - X_1^{\,q}$ at $(j,j_q)$.
--
--   This is the companion, for the branch of the special fibre through the cusp $0$, of the kernel computation along the branch through $\infty$: the reduction along the second branch is the coefficientwise reduction precomposed with the Fricke involution, and the local ideal it cuts out at the supersingular-type point $(a,a^q)$ is $(\varpi,\, j - j_q^{\,q})$, the Kronecker congruence factor conjugate to $j_q - j^{\,q}$. It feeds the crossing-exponent and node-coordinate analysis of place specialisations at level one, namely `crossingExponent_eq_placeWidth_mul_of_orderLawFixed_levelOne`, `exists_crossingPresentation_nodeIntegersOver_levelOne` and `exists_nodeCoordinates_nodeEquation_jWidth_of_eq_zero_or_eq_1728_levelOne`.
